              "summaryIds": [],
              "truncated": false
            },
            "sections": [
              {
                "id": "section-smoke-f094a2f1-2b36-4614-84ae-dc8919ce878f-0",
                "title": "1. Freshness and Cache-Control",
                "body": "When no cached entry exists, the browser fetches from network. If an entry exists, it checks **freshness** first:\n\n- `Cache-Control: max-age=3600` means reuse without contacting server for 3600 seconds.\n- `Cache-Control: no-cache` means always revalidate with server first.\n- `Cache-Control: no-store` means do not store at all.\n- `Expires` is the older fallback if `max-age` is absent.\n\nFresh = use immediately. Stale = must revalidate or refetch."
              },
              {
                "id": "section-smoke-f094a2f1-2b36-4614-84ae-dc8919ce878f-1",
                "title": "2. ETag revalidation",
                "body": "If cached response is stale but has validators, the browser sends a conditional request:\n\n- Server previously sent `ETag: \"abc123\"`\n- Browser sends `If-None-Match: \"abc123\"`\n- If content unchanged: server returns `304 Not Modified` with no body, browser reuses cache and updates freshness.\n- If changed: server returns `200 OK` with new body and new `ETag`.\n\n`Last-Modified` / `If-Modified-Since` works similarly, but `ETag` is more precise."
              },
              {
                "id": "section-smoke-f094a2f1-2b36-4614-84ae-dc8919ce878f-2",
                "title": "3. Small example",
                "body": "1. First visit to `/logo.png`:\n```http\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nCache-Control: max-age=60\nETag: \"v1\"\n```\n2. Second visit after 10s: fresh because age < 60, use cache, no request.\n3. Visit after 70s: stale, so browser sends:\n```http\nGET /logo.png\nIf-None-Match: \"v1\"\n```\nServer replies `304 Not Modified` if unchanged, or `200 OK` with `ETag: \"v2\"` if updated."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "position": [
          0,
